# The three reduction shapes, from source: §14 entry 28.
#
# `contractio.exsc` sums the SAME twenty `f32` values three times --
# `forma ordinata`, `forma arborea 8`, `forma arborea 4` -- and writes the
# three results as little-endian scaled `i64`s. The claim is that they are
# three DIFFERENT bit patterns and that each is exactly the bits §5.4's
# group-and-fold definition gives. Measured 2026-09-26:
#
#   ordinata   121209096   f32 0x41673021
#   arborea 8  121209080   f32 0x4167301F
#   arborea 4  121209088   f32 0x41673020
#
# Two ulps end to end, three distinct patterns. The declared shape is
# observable, which is why it has to be declared.
#
# THE INPUT is a committed file, not an `acies` literal, so that the
# oracle and the compiled program are fed the identical bytes by this
# harness and a mutation to the program cannot move the input with it:
#
#   python3 prototypes/contractio_oracle.py --gen > tests/data/contractio_viginti.bin
#
# 80 bytes, twenty little-endian signed 32-bit integers, each meaning
# n / 8388608.0 (2^-23: exact, so the input reaches the reduction
# unrounded and every rounding the program performs belongs to a shape).
#
# THE GOLDEN IS THE ORACLE'S, produced by the same script from that file
# and never by this compiler -- the not-our-own-bug check, the way
# pictura_triangulum/ uses prototypes/pictura_oracle.py:
#
#   python3 prototypes/contractio_oracle.py \
#       < tests/data/contractio_viginti.bin \
#       > tests/programs/contractio/expected.out
#
# 24 bytes. The oracle implements §5.4's "What a group computes, and how
# groups combine" paragraph in Python from the paragraph and nothing of
# the compiler, so byte-identity is two independent readings of §5.4
# landing on the same bits. (No `stdout=`: expected.out IS the reference,
# and naming both is run.sh's "which of the two governs?" failure.)
#
# MEASURED, 2026-09-26, by hand at 747fa30 plus the working tree's
# uncommitted §5.4 amendment, `build/exsc` of that content:
#
#   exsc aedifica --hospes x86_64-linux tests/programs/contractio/contractio.exsc -o c.asm   -> 0
#   fasmg c.asm c.bin                                                                        -> 0
#   c.bin < tests/data/contractio_viginti.bin > out                                          -> exit 0, empty stderr
#   cmp out tests/programs/contractio/expected.out                                           -> identical
#   tools/syscall-audit.sh c.bin                                                             -> PASS: read(0), write(1), exit_group
#
# MUTATIONS (run, on copies outside the tree; each changed the bytes):
#   * the middle loop's `forma arborea 8` -> `forma ordinata`: result 2
#     becomes result 1 (121209096 twice). The shape, and only the shape,
#     is what makes them differ.
#   * the first loop's `so = xs[i]` -> `so = xs[19 - i]`: result 1 alone
#     moves, to 121209072. `ordinata` is a fold IN INDEX ORDER, and the
#     order is part of it.
#   * the sign fix-up `si n ge 2147483648` disarmed: all three results
#     move together (to 17301213184) and become equal -- the four
#     negatives turned into values near 2^32, which dominate the sum so
#     completely that the shapes stop disagreeing. A fixture whose input
#     decode is wrong can accidentally stop testing what it is for; this
#     is that failure, observed.
# Edge inputs (run): 79 bytes -> exit 1, nothing written; empty stdin ->
# exit 1, nothing written; 81 bytes -> exit 0 and the same 24 bytes, the
# surplus byte never read.
#
# THE C BACKEND EMITS THIS MODULE, since 2026-09-27. This directory
# carried `c-exsc-exit=4` for two days, and that key was a finding
# rather than a workaround: `exsc --emitte c` exited 4 with
#
#   bfc: emitter: unsupported type: library mode holds an integer
#   (uN/iN), an address (ptr/ref/refc), a float (f32/f64) or a vector
#   float (vf32.N/vf64.N) and nothing else (c-backend.md D4, D8)
#
# -- the `red.F` handle type, refused one step before D4 rows 36-38's
# by-opcode-name refusal of `redinit`/`contrib`/`redfin` was ever
# reached, and the seven `tests/ir/red_*.ir` fixtures carried
# `c-emit-exit=4` for the same reason. So the differential phase could
# check PARITY of a refusal and nothing more. The C backend now lowers
# all three (c-backend.md rows 36-38); the key is gone and this
# directory is ELIGIBLE -- four builds, gcc and clang at -O0 and -O2,
# every one under `-fsanitize=undefined -fno-sanitize-recover=all`, each
# held to the same 24 bytes the reference is. Measured 2026-09-27: all
# four byte-identical to expected.out, which is the ORACLE's file and
# not this compiler's.
#
# WHAT THAT BUYS, and it is more than a fourth toolchain. The three
# results above are one f32 apart each; nothing about them survives a
# lowering that folds in a different order. So the differential phase
# now requires gcc and clang to build the same group trees and fold the
# same tails as the reference does. The C backend's reduction lowering
# emits ONE C STATEMENT PER PAIRWISE COMBINE for exactly this reason
# (emit_c.inc's reduction section, and prologue.c.in's contraction
# defence): a group tree emitted as one C expression would be a tree
# `-ffp-contract=fast` could fold, and spec 5.4's `contractio explicita`
# is the rule that forbids it. Two ulps of total spread is a small
# enough margin that a contracted tree would be caught right here.
#
# `cross=yes` -- AND BIG-ENDIAN IS WHERE THE FOLD ORDER STOPS BEING AN
# x86 FACT. The cross phase emits this unit for `--hospes
# mips64-none-o64`, cross-compiles it to big-endian MIPS-III with 32-bit
# addresses and runs it under `qemu-mipsn32`, against these same 24
# bytes. Two things differ on that row and neither may move a bit of the
# output: `mensura` is 32 bits there and 64 on the host, so the emitted
# unit's index arithmetic is a DIFFERENT call from the same source line
# (`exsi_*(…, 32)` against `exsi_*(…, 64)`, numerus_decimalis/'s finding);
# and clang soft-lowers every `f32` operation per operation, because
# MIPS-III has no SSE2 to lower to. The same 24 bytes on both rows is
# therefore the evidence that spec 5.4's group-and-fold order is a
# property of the LOWERING, which is what §14 entry 28's cross clause
# asserts and what ADR 0012's "the reference lowering is the definition"
# needs in order to mean anything portable.
#
# It could not be opted in before 2026-09-27: the cross phase goes
# through `--emitte c` as well (`exsc --hospes mips64-none-o64 --emitte
# c`, measured then: exit 4, the identical `red.F` message), so the key
# would have produced a phase failure rather than a run. Measured
# 2026-09-27, with the reduction lowering in: exit 0, 24 bytes, identical
# to expected.out -- the oracle's file. That retires the last `[UNTESTED]`
# leg of §14 entry 28.
TEST: expect-exit=0 stdin=tests/data/contractio_viginti.bin cross=yes
